      "content": "Coverage gap: this failure test (and the theme counterpart below) verifies the error banner appears and the selection rolls back, but nothing verifies the banner is cleared on a subsequent successful save. Both `LanguageSettingsViewModel.select` and `ThemeSettingsViewModel.select` reset `saveFailed`/`errorMessage` at the start of each attempt, and that recovery path is currently untested at every level. Consider making `failSave` mutable on the fakes, then after the rollback assertions set `failSave = false`, select again, and assert the `FAlert` disappears and the new mode is persisted. Also consider asserting the rolled-back rendered value text (e.g. the English label / `跟随系统`) here, mirroring the success tests' text assertions rather than relying solely on the mode-embedded row key.",
