      "thinking": "Confirmed: nowhere is it tested that the failure banner/error state clears after a subsequent successful save. Both `LanguageSettingsViewModel.select` and `ThemeSettingsViewModel.select` reset the error flag at the start, but neither the widget tests nor the view model tests verify this. The widget-level failure tests here are the natural place to cover banner dismissal on retry (asserting the FAlert's disappearance), because the view model tests only check booleans.\n\nThis is a legitimate test-coverage gap worth flagging (low/medium). The checklist explicitly asks \"do test cases cover boundary conditions?\" — the failure→recovery boundary is untested.\n\nAnything else? Let me re-check the diff once more to make sure I'm not missing anything…\n\nDiff details:\n\n1. `expect(find.text('Language'), ...)` → changed to `'App language'` — matches the new l10n string. No issue.\n\n2. After switching to zh in the language test: `expect(find.text('简体中文'), findsOneWidget);` — '简体中文' appears as the details text. If the menu were left open, the menu tile would also contain '简体中文' → 2 matches → findsOneWidget fails. So this also implicitly verifies the menu closes. Good.\n\n3. Theme test: `expect(find.text('跟随系统'), findsOneWidget);` is before opening the menu — matches the current-value detail. And `'浅色'/'深色'` being findsNothing confirms the options are collapsed. Good.\n\n4. New keys `'default-transcription-model-selected-background'` — asserting the gray selected-background wrapper exists. OK.\n\n5. Relaxed assertions for the font-scale test — replacing the positional stacking check with existence checks. Slightly weaker, but the layout changed (single FTile), and overflow is checked via takeException. Acceptable.\n\n6. Layout loop — added 872 and ledger key assertions. Good. Note: the `if (dimensions.$1.width \u003c 872)` branch — the boundary case at width 872 goes to else (two-column), which matches the inclusive `\u003e=` in fromWidth. OK.\n\n7. Fakes: