lled-back details text (e.g., that the 'English' label is restored)? The theme failure test could add `expect(find.text('跟随系统'), findsOneWidget)`, mirroring the success test's pattern. This would strengthen the UI-level verification beyond keys. Could mention it as a suggestion in the same comment. Hmm, let me keep the feedback focused: one comment about the recovery/clear coverage gap (medium/low), optionally suggesting adding an assertion on the rendered current-value text. \n\nActually, let me double-check one more point in the language failure test — does the Application widget display zh text for the alert? The test only asserts the presence of FAlert within the language-section and doesn't check the alert text. No issue.\n\nOne more check about the \"模型不可用错误显示在新会议默认章节\" test: it asserts `find.text('模型设置未完成')` findsOneWidget. Alert title = l10n.modelSettingsIncomplete. OK.\n\nAlso — a potential issue with dispose ordering in this test: `viewModel.dispose(); await installations.dispose();` — no issue.\n\nNow let me also think about `tester.pump()` after `await viewModel.selectDefault(...)`. The errorMessage path notifies listeners synchronously inside selectDefault's async body. `await` guarantees completion. Then `pump()` rebuilds the ListenableBuilder. Works. But hmm — could there be pending microtasks or frames that pumpAndSettle would clear, e.g., an FAlert animation? `pump()` renders one frame; find works immediately. No issue.\n\nAlso considering: in the failure tests, after tapping `language-mode-simplifiedChinese`, is there any timing where the menu-close animation keeps pumping? pumpAndSettle handles it.\n\nFinal decision: file one comment on the language failure test (also applies to theme): note the missing coverage for \"banner clears on successful retry\" + optionally suggest asserting the rolled-back value text. Category: test. Severity: low.\n\nLet me write the comment concisely. Reference the language test's location:\n\n```dart\n    expect(languageMode.value, AppLanguageMode.english);\n    expect(\n      find.byKey(const ValueKey('language-setting-row-english')),\n      findsOneWidget,\n    );\n```\n\nHmm, but the comment should target new code. The entire test is new. I'll target the end of the language failure test's assertion block.\n\nOne more check — is there a way for the test to verify recovery with the current fake design? Yes: make failSave mutable (a non-final `bool failSave`), tap a row → fail → then set `failSave = false`, select again, and assert the FAlert disappears and the value is saved. This is actionable.\n\nSeverity: low (coverage gap, not a bug).\n\nLet me write the final comment. One more quick scan of the remaining diff hunks I haven't reviewed carefully:\n\n- `+ (const Size(872, 760), const ValueKey('settings-two-column')),` — duplicate check: 872 → two-column; 1024 → two-column. The 872 test name: '872 宽度使用对应设置布局且不溢出'. No issue.\n\n- Fakes with failSave — throws before assignment, good; `savedMode` remains null.\n\nI think there's just one comment. Let me phrase it.",
