      "content": "`maxLines: 2` caps the paragraph's layout height at two lines, and with `TextOverflow.visible` any additional wrapped lines are painted outside that box — over the tile padding and into neighboring content — without raising a layout exception. At 2.0 text scale (and in the narrow two-column widths near the 872px breakpoint, where prefix/details/check squeeze the subtitle column), the lock description (e.g. EN: \"Future meetings only; locked after recording starts—no automatic switching.\") can easily need more than two lines. This conflicts with the requirements that the model-lock description be fully displayed and that 2.0 scaling not overflow; note the existing 2.0-scale test only checks `tester.takeException()`, which cannot catch visible-overflow painting. If full display is intended, let the text wrap naturally (drop `maxLines`/`overflow`) so the tile grows to fit.",
