      "thinking": "I've completed the overall review of this file. Now let me nail down my findings.\n\n**Findings to report:**\n\n1. **[Medium · Bug] `_SettingsValueRow` subtitle: `maxLines: 2, overflow: TextOverflow.visible`** — The model lock description (\"Future meetings only; locked after recording starts—no automatic switching.\" / \"只影响后续新会议；录音后锁定且不自动切换。\") is limited to 2 lines in layout, but overflowing lines are drawn outside the layout box and visually overlap with adjacent content at 2.0× text scale or in narrow columns (e.g., 2-column layout at 872px, where the subtitle column is squeezed by the prefix icon, details text, and the check suffix). This conflicts with the explicit requirements that the lock description must be shown in full and that nothing should overflow at 2.0 scale. Also, the existing 2.0-scale test relies on `tester.takeException()`, which cannot detect `TextOverflow.visible` painting overflow. If full visibility is required, I suggest removing `maxLines`/`overflow` so the tile stretches to fit.\n\n2. **[Low · Maintainability] Combined section title when only one subsection is present** — `appearanceLanguageTitle` (\"Appearance and language\" / \"外观与语言\") is always used even if only one of themeSettings/languageSettings is non-null. The widget's public API accepts these as nullable, and tests exercise those configurations too. The heading would misdescribe the contents. Production currently always passes both, so this is low priority. I suggest picking the title based on which subsection is present, or asserting both-or-neither.\n\n3. **[Low · Maintainability] ColoredBox wrapping `FTile(selected: true)`** — `_PreferenceTile` relies on `FTile(selected:)` alone to convey the selected state, which suggests forui already draws a background when selected. If FTile paints an opaque selected background, the outer `ColoredBox(color: context.theme.colors.secondary)` never shows up and the intended grayscale background is actually coming from forui's default, not from this code. Worth verifying (e.g., remove FTile's own selected background, or leave `selected: false` and let ColoredBox handle it). Given that `secondary` is grayscale in both themes (0xFFEFEFEC / 0xFF202020), the intent is right but the mechanism might be redundant. Low priority.\n\nShould I flag all three? Finding 1 is solid. Findings 2 and 3 are lower-confidence / more speculative. The instructions say to stay objective and avoid speculation. Regarding finding 3, I verified that `_PreferenceTile` uses selected without ColoredBox. That's factual backing that FTile draws a selected state itself. I'll phrase it as \"verify that ColoredBox is actually visible / consider removing redundancy.\" This is legitimate review feedback (maintainability), so I'll include it as low.\n\nRegarding finding 2 — in production both are always passed. Flagging might be noise, but the widget's API supports the nullable combination and the tests exercise it too. The \"Appearance and language\" heading when only language is shown is a small accuracy/maintainability observation. I'll include it as low.\n\nAlso, let me re-check the breakpoint: requirement \"桌面双栏从内容宽度 840（视口 872，页面 16px 内边距）\" (desktop 2-column from content width 840 (viewport 872, page 16px padding)) — Verified: `wideLayoutMinWidth = 840`, `spaceMd = 16` is applied to both sides by AppPageBody, AppResponsiveBuilder is inside it → matches. Tests cover 872. Good, no issue here.\n\nAnd managedRadio rollback — I verified the view model does optimistic-update-then-rollback and tests cover it. No issue.\n\nOne more consideration about finding 1: is there a possibility that `FTile` imposes unbounded constraints and there's no overlap? Even if the subtitle column has unbounded height, maxLines: 2 still limits the paragraph height to 2 lines, and overflow gets drawn below the paragraph box, inside the tile (above the tile's bottom padding) or crossing over. The overlap risk is still real. Even in the English desktop 2-column case at 1.0 scale, about 404px wide column: tile padding ~16×2 + prefix 24 + spacing ~8 + details \"SenseVoice...\" probably 100–130 + suffix 24 → subtitle width ~200px → English description at body.sm (13px) is about 30 chars per line → 77 chars → 3 lines \u003e 2 → overlap even at 1.0× scale! Hmm, this depends on the actual width forui gives the subtitle column (details might be aligned to top-right). This strengthens finding 1.\n\nActually, wait, let me reconsider: does the subtitle's width exclude details? Typical forui FTile layout (from forui docs): tile is prefix | title+subtitle column | details | suffix, with the middle column Expanded. So yes, the subtitle's width excludes details. At English 1.0 scale, single column 760px: 760-32(pad)-24(icon)-… subtitle width is probably ~600px → about 90 chars per line → 1 line, no issue. Two columns at 872: column ~404 → subtitle width ~250–280 → about 40 chars per line → 2 lines, just fits. Two columns at 2.0 scale: won't fit. So this issue mainly manifests at high text scale and narrow two-column widths — exactly the requirement boundary (\"2.0 字体缩放不得溢出\" / \"no overflow at 2.0× text scale\"). Still valid as medium.\n\nOK, let me write the comments. Three total: 1 medium, 2 low.\n\nFor comment 1, I'll suggest removing maxLines/overflow:\n\n```dart\nsubtitle: Text(description),\n```\n\nThat will fully wrap inside the tile and satisfy \"完整显示\" (display in full).\n\nI'll phrase the content concisely and factually.",
