      "thinking": "I've completed the overall review of this file. Now let me nail down my findings.\n\n**Findings to report:**\n\n1. **[Medium · Bug] `_SettingsValueRow` subtitle: `maxLines: 2, overflow: TextOverflow.visible`** — The model lock description (\"Future meetings only; locked after recording starts—no automatic switching.\" / \"只影响后续新会议；录音后锁定且不自动切换。\") is limited to 2 lines in layout, but overflowing lines are drawn outside the layout box and visually overlap with adjacent content at 2.0× text scale or in narrow columns (e.g., 2-column layout at 872px, where the subtitle column is squeezed by the prefix icon, details text, and the check suffix). This conflicts with the explicit requirements that the lock description must be shown in full and that nothing should overflow at 2.0 scale. Also, the existing 2.0-scale test relies on `tester.takeException()`, which cannot detect `TextOverflow.visible` painting overflow. If full visibility is required, I suggest removing `maxLines`/`overflow` so the tile stretches to fit.\n\n2. **[Low · Maintainability] Combined section title when only one subsection is present** — `appearanceLanguageTitle` (\"Appearance and language\" / \"外观与语言\") is always used even if only one of themeSettings/languageSettings is non-null. The widget's public API accepts these as nullable, and tests exercise those configurations too. The heading would misdescribe the contents. Production currently always passes both, so this is low priority. I suggest picking the title based on which subsection is present, or asserting both-or-neither.\n\n3. **[Low · Maintainability] ColoredBox wrapping `FTile(selected: true)`** — `_PreferenceTile` relies on `FTile(selected:)` alone to convey the selected state, which suggests forui already draws a background when selected. If FTile paints an opaque selected background, the outer `ColoredBox(color: context.theme.colors.secondary)` never shows up and the intended grayscale background is actually coming from forui's default, not from this code. Worth verifying (e.g., remove FTile's own selected background, or leave `selected: false` and let ColoredBox handle it). Given that `secondary` is grayscale in both themes (0xFFEFEFEC / 0xFF202020), the intent is right but the mechanism might be redundant. Low priority.\n\nShould I flag all three? Finding 1 is solid. Findings 2 and 3 are lower-confidence / more speculative. The instructions say to stay objective and avoid speculation. Regarding finding 3, I verified that `_PreferenceTile` uses selected without ColoredBox. That's factual backing that FTile draws a selected state itself. I'll phrase it as \"verify that ColoredBox is actually visible / consider removing redundancy.\" This is legitimate review feedback (maintainability), so I'll include it as low.\n\nRegarding finding 2 — in production both are always passed. Flagging might be noise, but the widget's API supports the nullable combination and the tests exercise it too. The \"Appearance and language\" heading when only language is shown is a small accuracy/maintainability observation. I'll include it as low.\n\nAlso, let me re-check the breakpoint: requirement \"桌面双栏从内容宽度 840（视口 872，页面 16px 内边距）\" (desktop 2-column from content width 840 (viewport 872, page 16px padding)) — Verified: `wideLayoutMinWidth = 840`, `spaceMd = 16` is applied to both sides by AppPageBody, AppResponsiveBuilder is inside it → matches. Tests cover 872. Good, no issue here.\n\nAnd managedRadio rollback — I verified the view model does optimistic-update-then-rollback and tests cover it. No issue.\n\nOne more consideration about finding 1: is there a possibility that `FTile` imposes unbounded constraints and there's no overlap? Even if the subtitle column has unbounded height, maxLines: 2 still limits the paragraph height to 2 lines, and overflow gets drawn below the paragraph box, inside the tile (above the tile's bottom padding) or crossing over. The overlap risk is still real. Even in the English desktop 2-column case at 1.0 scale, about 404px wide column: tile padding ~16×2 + prefix 24 + spacing ~8 + details \"SenseVoice...\" probably 100–130 + suffix 24 → subtitle width ~200px → English description at body.sm (13px) is about 30 chars per line → 77 chars → 3 lines \u003e 2 → overlap even at 1.0× scale! Hmm, this depends on the actual width forui gives the subtitle column (details might be aligned to top-right). This strengthens finding 1.\n\nActually, wait, let me reconsider: does the subtitle's width exclude details? Typical forui FTile layout (from forui docs): tile is prefix | title+subtitle column | details | suffix, with the middle column Expanded. So yes, the subtitle's width excludes details. At English 1.0 scale, single column 760px: 760-32(pad)-24(icon)-… subtitle width is probably ~600px → about 90 chars per line → 1 line, no issue. Two columns at 872: column ~404 → subtitle width ~250–280 → about 40 chars per line → 2 lines, just fits. Two columns at 2.0 scale: won't fit. So this issue mainly manifests at high text scale and narrow two-column widths — exactly the requirement boundary (\"2.0 字体缩放不得溢出\" / \"no overflow at 2.0× text scale\"). Still valid as medium.\n\nOK, let me write the comments. Three total: 1 medium, 2 low.\n\nFor comment 1, I'll suggest removing maxLines/overflow:\n\n```dart\nsubtitle: Text(description),\n```\n\nThat will fully wrap inside the tile and satisfy \"完整显示\" (display in full).\n\nI'll phrase the content concisely and factually.",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "lib/ui/features/settings/views/model_settings_view.dart",
      "content": "Every `_SettingsSection` draws both a top and a bottom rule (`Border.symmetric(horizontal: ...)`), while `_SettingsLedger` still inserts a `SizedBox(height: spaceLg)` gap between consecutive sections. The net effect is two parallel divider lines between any two adjacent sections (previous section's bottom rule + next section's top rule, separated by the gap) — in the single-column continuous ledger this happens at every section junction. This deviates from the requirement's “共享边缘和分隔线” (adjacent groups should share a single edge), and regresses from the old single `topRule` separator. Consider rendering only one border side per section (e.g. bottom-only, with the ledger supplying spacing) or collapsing the gap so adjacent rules merge into one shared line.",
      "existing_code": "        DecoratedBox(\n          decoration: BoxDecoration(\n            border: Border.symmetric(\n              horizontal: BorderSide(\n                color: theme.colors.border,\n                width: appStyle.dividerWidth,\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n          child: child,\n        ),",
      "start_line": 1049,
      "end_line": 1059,
      "thinking": "All identifiers exist. Now, finalizing the review.\n\nThe remaining new issue I'm confident about:\n\n**Double divider lines between adjacent sections**: `_SettingsSection` draws both a top and bottom border via `Border.symmetric(horizontal: ...)`, and `_SettingsLedger` inserts a `spaceLg` gap between consecutive sections. As a result, between any two adjacent sections there are two parallel divider lines (the previous section's bottom rule + the next section's top rule) with a gap between them. This deviates from the \"shared edges\" (shared edge / a single divider shared between adjacent groups) requirement, and it also regresses from the previous single-`topRule` design. Recommendation: draw only one side per section (e.g., top-only border and omit the spacing gap, or bottom-only and no line on the last item), or remove the gap so the borders overlap into a single shared line.\n\nI'll flag this on `_SettingsSection`'s border code (or `_SettingsLedger`). The most appropriate place is either the `Border.symmetric(horizontal: ...)` block of `_SettingsSection`, or the gap line of `_SettingsLedger`. I'll comment on `_SettingsSection`'s border.\n\nSeverity: medium. Category: style (visual design consistency). Hmm — actually it could also be \"correctness\" against the requirement, but it's a visual matter so \"style\" is appropriate.\n\nAnything else? Let me think whether `_SettingsTileGroup`'s `RoundedRectangleBorder` and `FTileGroup` might have issues — they intentionally replace rounded corners with sharp corners to match the ledger. No issue.\n\nAnother consideration: in `_MeetingDefaultsSection`, the error `FAlert` is placed inside the bordered area (between the top border and the tile group). Visually it's inside the ruled box — acceptable.\n\nAlso, in the combined appearance-language `_SettingsSection`, the child Column includes appearance's `DecoratedBox` with a bottom border `dividerWidth`, then the language section. OK.\n\nAlso, in single-column mode, does `_RemoteDiagnosticsSection` get an `FSwitch` with vertical padding? The section child is FSwitch directly inside the bordered DecoratedBox — it might touch the border without padding, but this is a pre-existing layout (previously also `_SettingsSection`'s child). No issue.\n\nI'll submit the one comment about the double divider lines. Should I also mention the issue of the first section drawing a top border at the top of the page? This is included in the symmetric design and is part of the same \"boxed\" look. I'll keep the comment focused.\n\nLet me write the code comment using existing code lines from the diff:\n\n```\n        DecoratedBox(\n          decoration: BoxDecoration(\n            border: Border.symmetric(\n              horizontal: BorderSide(\n                color: theme.colors.border,\n                width: appStyle.dividerWidth,\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n          child: child,\n        ),\n```\n\nIn the diff, the following is shown within `_SettingsSection`:\n```\n+        DecoratedBox(\n+          decoration: BoxDecoration(\n+            border: Border.symmetric(\n+              horizontal: BorderSide(\n+                color: theme.colors.border,\n+                width: appStyle.dividerWidth,\n+              ),\n+            ),\n+          ),\n+          child: child,\n+        ),\n```\n\nI'll target this block.",
      "category": "style",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "test/ui/features/settings/views/model_settings_view_test.dart",
      "content": "The model resource layout was reworked here (name is now the FTile title and `_ModelResourceStatus` moved into `details`), but the sibling test '手机宽度下资源大小不被维护操作挤成两行' (lines 359-361 of this file) was not updated to match. The new `_ModelResourceLedger` renders size + version as a single `FTile` subtitle joined with a hard `\\n`, so `find.textContaining('239.5 MB')` now matches a deliberately two-line text (≈ 2 × 15 × 1.5 = 45px with touch typography), while that test still asserts `tester.getSize(metadata).height, lessThan(30)`. That assertion will either fail, or — if the tile slot constrains the subtitle to one line — silently pass while the version line is clipped, contradicting the intent that the model metadata is shown in full. Please update that test alongside these layout assertions (e.g., bound the height to the two-line design and assert both the size and version strings are present/visible).",
      "existing_code": "    expect(find.byKey(const ValueKey('model-resource-name')), findsOneWidget);\n    expect(find.byKey(const ValueKey('model-resource-status')), findsOneWidget);",
      "start_line": 391,
      "end_line": 392,
      "thinking": "Confirmed: The test at lines 359–361 hasn't been changed and asserts that `find.textContaining('239.5 MB')` has `height \u003c 30`.\n\nIn the new implementation, the only widget containing \"239.5 MB\" is the FTile's subtitle inside `_ModelResourceLedger`:\n\n```dart\nsubtitle: Text(\n  '${_languageLabel(...)} · ${_decimalMegabytes(...)}\\n'\n  '${l10n.modelVersionAutoLanguage(...)}',\n),\n```\n\nThis is explicitly a 2-line text (hard `\\n`). With touch=true, body.sm = fontSize 15, height 1.5 → one line ≈ 22.5px → two lines ≈ 45px \u003e 30.\n\nTwo possible outcomes:\n1. FTile doesn't restrict the subtitle → renders as 2 lines → height ≈ 45px → this unmodified assertion fails.\n2. FTile restricts the subtitle to 1 line → the second line (version info) gets truncated → contradicts the \"完整显示 (fully display)\" requirement, and the earlier design intent in the diff's comment as well… In that case, the assertion would pass.\n\nEither way, the fact that the unmodified test wasn't revisited is a real inconsistency introduced by this PR. I'll add a comment anchored to the closest newly-added code — the updated model-resource assertions in the font-scaling test.\n\nAlright, now I'll write the comment.",
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
